From: AX50 OpenWrt bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] wave: allow exclusive monitor open before channel selection

cfg80211 only dispatches set_monitor_channel while at least one monitor is
running.  The native cold-radio channel is initially unset, so requiring
SET_CHAN in ndo_open prevents the standard open-then-tune sequence.

Keep the whole-card claim and leave carrier, RX and TX stopped when no usable
saved channel exists.  The first channel request on the running monitor uses
the existing typed activation path; saved-channel reopen is unchanged.

--- a/wireless/driver/linux/cfg80211.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/linux/cfg80211.c
@@ -740,6 +740,15 @@
   if (res != MTLK_ERR_OK)
     return _mtlk_df_mtlk_to_linux_error_code(res);
   mon->claimed = true;
+  /* cfg80211 accepts monitor channel selection only with a running monitor.
+   * A cold radio has no channel yet: reserve the exclusive owner, but keep
+   * RX/TX stopped until the first successful set_monitor_channel request.
+   * A usable saved channel still resumes through the ordinary open path. */
+  if (!cfg80211_chandef_valid(&mon->chandef) ||
+      !cfg80211_chandef_usable(mon->wdev.wiphy, &mon->chandef, IEEE80211_CHAN_DISABLED)) {
+    wv_cfg80211_monitor_suspend(mon);
+    return 0;
+  }
   res = wave_monitor_start_channel(mon);
   if (res) {
     wave_monitor_stop_hardware(mon);
